WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.449 --> 00:00:07.049
This is Michael Spavor, doing what he does
best: bringing foreign athletes to Pyongyang,

00:00:07.049 --> 00:00:09.930
to play the North Korean hockey team.

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:14.269
He is a Canadian businessman with a cultural
exchange company based in the northern Chinese

00:00:14.269 --> 00:00:16.670
city of Dangdong.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:22.680
He is also the man behind the unsual friendship
between US basketball star Dennis Rodman and

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:26.020
North Korean leader Kim Jong Un.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:30.400
Spavor is possibly one of the best-connected
business people in secretive North Korea,

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.310
and now, nobody is exactly sure where he is.

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:39.640
Before Beijing confirmed it was investigating
Spavor, Canada's foreign minister confirmed

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.580
something was amiss.

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:59.899
We are aware of a Canadian who got in touch
with us because he was being asked questions

00:00:59.899 --> 00:01:01.470
by Chinese authorities.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:02.470
We have not been able to make contact with
him since he let us know about this.

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:03.470
We are working very hard to ascertain his
whereabouts and we have also raised this case

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:04.470
with the Chinese authorities.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:05.470
We are in touch with his family.

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:08.439
Spavor also uses his base in China to promote
investment in North Korea.

00:01:08.439 --> 00:01:17.859
But China now says he is a security risk.

